  "caption": "Quinn couldn't check a blind spot without turning the whole body like a fridge. Add a sore neck, a cranky shoulder and an achy back, each treated separately, and it felt like whack-a-mole.\n\nKay explained that a stiff upper back can make its neighbours overwork, so the neck, shoulders and lower back pick up the slack. It's often worth loosening the middle, not just the sore bits.\n\nWhat can help: testing seated rotation, foam roller extensions, thread-the-needle, and shoulder-blade strengthening, with 5–10 minutes most days.\n\nGet it checked after a fall or knock, if symptoms affect both arms or legs, with fever, weight loss or severe night pain, or with chest pain or breathlessness.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
